01:03:55.160 --> 01:04:04.480
RAG calling in—calling in link chain as well as&nbsp;
PDFs that are specific to ASL&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:04.480 --> 01:04:08.791
learning that get chunked and transformed&nbsp;in a vector-dimension space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:09.260 --> 01:04:18.440
Now as you can see here, this is a hand-pose estimation extraction using the media pipe library.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:18.440 --> 01:04:26.400
So you can see A, B, and C. And here's our platform,&nbsp;
where you can—there are different modules to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:26.400 --> 01:04:33.320
alphabets signs as well as sentences. We even&nbsp;
have—we even have our real-time ASL practice, so in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:33.320 --> 01:04:38.080
real time to capture the sign that you are&nbsp;
actually—the letter that you're actually signing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:38.080 --> 01:04:43.760
and give you the accuracy for that. So here's an&nbsp;
example of us using the media pipe library to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:43.760 --> 01:04:50.480
actually extract all of the hand key-points.&nbsp;Here are some videos where they're over—&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:50.480 --> 01:04:55.640
over hundreds of words that you can actually view&nbsp;
to learn each of the hand-signing frames.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:57.000 --> 01:05:03.080
Now, this is our—this is our proprietary RAG and&nbsp;
the way we've trained this is we—we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:03.080 --> 01:05:09.160
we've collected a variety of&nbsp;
PDFs that that are essentially manuals for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:09.160 --> 01:05:15.480
ASL learning. Potentially in the future,&nbsp;
we—we would want to incorporate things like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:15.480 --> 01:05:21.160
YouTube transcriptions that can actually be, that&nbsp;
that can actually be transformed and and embedded&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:21.160 --> 01:05:29.240
within our vector-dimension model.&nbsp;
Now in the future, this doesn't—ASL&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:29.240 --> 01:05:36.240
doesn't just—hand pose estimation doesn't&nbsp;
just have to be have to be localized to ASL.&nbsp;

01:05:36.240 --> 01:05:41.840
There are plenty of other opportunities for&nbsp;
for human pose estimation—including&nbsp;&nbsp;

